cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  aee-vocabulary: a canonical term registry for adversarial-execution
  evidence claims
message: >-
  If a term or crosswalk-match verdict from this registry is cited, cite the
  released version rather than the branch. A registry is a moving target
  until it is tagged.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Gilda
    given-names: Sankalp
    email: sankalp.gilda@gmail.com
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3645-4501'
repository-code: https://github.com/astrogilda/aee-vocabulary
abstract: >-
  A closed, versioned vocabulary for terms that describe adversarial-execution
  evidence claims -- observation vantage, observation directness, containment
  posture, coverage denominators, and related evidence-quality dimensions.
  Independent implementations file crosswalks declaring how their own emitted
  claims map onto these terms. Companion project to aee-conformance
  (https://github.com/astrogilda/aee-conformance), which hosts the predicate
  spec this vocabulary describes and its conformance vector suite.
license: Apache-2.0
